+## The dashboard
+
+ONE self-contained HTML file — inline CSS/JS, zero external requests (no CDN,
+no web fonts, no remote images), with a JSON snapshot of your data baked in.
+Two ways to use it:
+
+- **Live mode (buttons on)** — `./shopkeep.sh start` (or `python3
+  shopkeep-web.py`), then open `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. The server binds
+  127.0.0.1 ONLY, reads the CSVs for display, and forwards every change to
+  `./shopkeep.sh` as a subprocess — **shopkeep.sh stays the ONLY writer to the
+  CSVs**; Python never writes them (one narrow exception: see `/api/import`).
+- **Read-only snapshot** — double-click `shopkeep-dashboard.html` (`file://`).
+  A banner reminds you it is a snapshot. Every mutating button is REMOVED from
+  the page in this mode (hidden, not greyed out), so a snapshot can never
+  change your data.
+
+### Every button, and what it really does
+
+| Tab | Button | HTTP call | Runs |
+|-----|--------|-----------|------|
+| Billing | Charge bill | `POST /api/bill` | `bill` |
+| Billing | Scan (camera / photo) | — (browser decodes locally) | fills the bill lines for you |
+| Billing | Void a bill | `POST /api/void` | `void` |
+| Billing | Return items | `POST /api/return` | `return` |
+| Billing | UPI QR (after a saved bill) | `GET /api/upiqr` | `upi-qr` |
+| Products | + Add product | `POST /api/add` | `add` |
+| Products | + Stock (per row) | `POST /api/restock` | `restock` |
+| Products | Edit (per row) | `POST /api/edit` | `edit` |
+| Products | Remove (per row) | `POST /api/remove` | `remove` |
+| Products | + Category | `POST /api/category-add` | `category add` |
+| Products | + Combo tray | `POST /api/tray-add` | `tray add` |
+| Products | Remove tray | `POST /api/tray-remove` | `tray remove` |
+| Reports | date range, filters, stock value | — (computed in your browser from `/api/*.json`) | — |
+| Data & backup | Backup now | `POST /api/backup` | `backup` |
+| Data & backup | Export CSVs | `POST /api/export` | `export` |
+| Data & backup | Download an exported CSV | `GET /api/download/<file>` | — |
+| Data & backup | Check file / Import for real | `POST /api/import` | `import --dry-run` / `import` |
+| Settings | Save settings | `POST /api/config` | `config` |
+
+Safety rails you can feel: every button shows a busy state and disables itself
+while working (a double-click can never charge two bills — server-side `flock`
+makes that a guarantee, not a promise); destructive actions ask in plain words
+("This cancels bill #5 and puts the items back in stock. Continue?"); success
+is a big green box; errors are a plain red box that shows **exactly** what
+shopkeep.sh said — never a stack trace.
+
+### Languages
+
+23 languages in the terminal (`./shopkeep.sh lang hi`). The dashboard's
+Settings dropdown offers English, हिन्दी, தமிழ், తెలుగు, বাংলা; every other
+language falls back to English for the few strings it lacks. Setting a language
+in Settings saves it to `shopkeep.conf` and it sticks for the terminal too.
