+The dashboard refreshes ALL panels from the read endpoints after every
+mutation.
+
+**Read endpoints**
+
+| Endpoint | Returns |
+|----------|---------|
+| `GET /` | the dashboard itself, regenerated live |
+| `GET /api/products.json` | products.csv as JSON |
+| `GET /api/bills.json` | bills.csv as JSON |
+| `GET /api/categories.json` | categories.csv as JSON |
+| `GET /api/trays.json` | trays.csv as JSON |
+| `GET /api/inventorylog.json` | last 100 audit rows, newest first |
+| `GET /api/config.json` | shopkeep.conf (read-only) + language list |
+| `GET /api/download/<file>` | an export from `shopkeep-data/exports/` (filename resolved against the REAL exports listing — path traversal is rejected) |
+| `GET /api/upiqr?amount=&note=` | UPI QR — base64 PNG when zint exists, else SVG |
+
+**Mutating endpoints**
+
+| Endpoint | Body | Runs |
+|----------|------|------|
+| `POST /api/bill` | `{"lines":[..],"phone":..,"discount":..}` | `bill` |
+| `POST /api/add` | `{"name","price","qty"[,"barcode","threshold","desc","type","expiry","hsn"]}` | `add` |
+| `POST /api/edit` | `{"barcode"[,"name","price","threshold","desc","type","expiry","hsn"]}` | `edit` |
+| `POST /api/restock` | `{"barcode","qty"[,"reason"]}` (qty must be > 0) | `restock` |
+| `POST /api/remove` | `{"barcode"[,"reason"]}` | `remove` |
+| `POST /api/tray-add` | `{"barcode","name","items":"bc:qty,bc:qty"}` | `tray add` |
+| `POST /api/tray-remove` | `{"barcode"}` | `tray remove` |
+| `POST /api/category-add` | `{"name"[,"emoji"]}` | `category add` |
+| `POST /api/void` | `{"billNo"}` | `void` |
+| `POST /api/return` | `{"billNo"[,"qtys":"bc:qty,...","reason"]}` | `return` |
+| `POST /api/backup` | `{}` | `backup` |
+| `POST /api/export` | `{"scope": all\|products\|bills\|inventory_log\|trays\|categories}` → adds `"files":[...]` for download links | `export` |
+| `POST /api/config` | `{"key","value"}` or `{"settings":{...}}` (allowlist: shop_name, gstin, address, phone, default_threshold, lang, upi_vpa) | `config` |
+| `POST /api/import` | `{"csv":"<file text>","dryRun":true\|false}` — the REAL `shopkeep.sh import` validator report comes back verbatim | `import [--dry-run]` |
+
+Import is the ONE place Python touches a CSV file it will hand to the shell:
+the upload is written to a system temp dir **outside** `shopkeep-data/`, passed
+to `shopkeep.sh import` (which remains the only writer of your data files),
+and deleted immediately. Validation lives in the shell script — the GUI never
+re-implements it, so what you see in "Check file" is exactly what will happen.
+
