+| Symptom | Meaning / fix |
+|---------|---------------|
+| `start` says **Already running** | The dashboard is already up — open http://127.0.0.1:8000 |
+| `start` says the port did not open | Something else has port 8000 — stop it, or see `shopkeep-data/server.log` for the actual error |
+| `stop` says "Not running (no pid file)" | Nothing to stop — safe, ignore |
+| Browser did not open | No GUI/browser on this machine — open http://127.0.0.1:8000 yourself |
+| Scan button shows a hint about zbar | `sudo apt install zbar-tools` (one time; needs internet) |
+| Camera scan does nothing in the dashboard | The browser lacks the BarcodeDetector API — use **Chrome or Edge**, or use `scan --image` from the terminal |
+| Dashboard shows old data after you edited CSVs by hand | Regenerate: `./shopkeep.sh web`, or just refresh the live page |
+| Buttons are missing entirely | You opened the `file://` snapshot — run `./shopkeep.sh start` for the live dashboard |
+| **WSL2** | Keep the shopkeep folder on the Linux filesystem (ext4), NOT `/mnt/c/...` — flock and atomic rename are unreliable on Windows drives. Git Bash / macOS lack `flock` (exit 2). From Windows, open http://127.0.0.1:8000 — WSL2 forwards localhost automatically |
+
+## Known limitations (honest)
+
+- **Camera scanning needs `zbar-tools`** — a one-time `sudo apt install`.
+  Without it, camera/image scan shows a hint instead of failing silently.
+- **Dashboard camera scan needs Chrome/Edge** (BarcodeDetector API). Firefox
+  and Safari get an inline hint. No third-party decoder is ever embedded.
+- **The localhost server has no auth** — it is for the shop's own laptop.
+  Never port-forward 8000; never run it on a shared network machine.
+- **`file://` dashboard is a static snapshot** — buttons are removed so it
+  cannot change data; it also shows the data as of generation time.
+- **CSV scale ceilings** — comfortable to tens of thousands of rows; this is
+  deliberately not a database.
+- **Pre-1.3.0 bills lack SALE rows** in inventory_log — the 1:1 SELL↔SALE
+  reconcile holds from v1.3.0 onward.
+- **94 i18n keys are unwired** in some non-en languages (menus fall back to
+  English for those strings) — wiring them is proposed for v1.5.
+- **Single-machine design** — no multi-store sync, no multi-terminal UI (the
+  data model is concurrency-safe so a UI can be added without migration).
 - No taxes / customer CRM / multi-currency (per-line and bill-level discounts
-  ARE supported).
