+## Changelog — v1.4.0 (vs v1.3.0)
+
+### Fixed
+- **Saved language was never read back** (v1.3.0 bug): `lang=hi` in
+  shopkeep.conf was ignored at startup, so menus, receipts and the dashboard
+  always booted English. Now read back, validated, and honoured everywhere —
+  the dashboard language dropdown updates the terminal too.
+- **`stop` could orphan the server**: the pidfile captured the launcher's
+  wrapper subshell instead of the python process, so `stop` killed the wrapper
+  and left the real server alive. The launcher now `exec`s into python and the
+  pidfile holds the real pid.
+- UPI QR never appeared after a dashboard bill (bill-number "0003" vs "3"
+  mismatch when matching the receipt).
+- The `file://` snapshot could still show three live-only controls (billing,
+  void/return, add-product) — snapshot purity audited to zero mutating nodes.
+- Four report headings ignored the selected language.
+- Robustness pass (5A/5B): the interactive menu no longer dies when a handler
+  is cancelled or fails; `config` rejects unknown keys instead of writing them
+  silently; `-h` no longer omits `publish`; new-subcommand usage errors return
+  cleanly instead of exiting mid-process; `gen-qr` no longer produces
+  `x.svg.svg` for SVG outputs; emoji category matching no longer confuses
+  "ice cream" with soap.
+
+### Added
+- **Full button dashboard**: 5 tabs (Billing / Products / Reports /
+  Data & backup / Settings), big touch buttons, plain-word confirms, verbatim
+  error text, busy states, auto-refresh — backed by 14 POST endpoints and
+  read-only JSON endpoints (see the HTTP API section).
+- **Scan**: camera (`zbarcam`) and image (`zbarimg`) barcode decoding,
+  `scan --image FILE [--bill]`, and `c:`/`i:` input prefixes inside the
+  interactive bill.
+- **quickbill**: one-shot argv billing on the same engine as `bill`
+  (byte-identical rows, proven by selftest).
+- **import**: bulk CSV product loading — all-or-nothing, `--dry-run` report,
+  `--template`; the same validator powers the dashboard's Check/Import flow.
+- **report <start> <end>**: range sales report on the same core as `summary`
+  (totals provably equal the sum of per-day summaries).
+- **export**: Excel-safe CSV copies into `shopkeep-data/exports/` (formula
+  injection guarded; raw CSVs untouched) + dashboard download buttons.
+- **upi-qr** + `upi_vpa` config: UPI intent QR on receipts, via
+  `upi-qr <amount>`, in the dashboard after each saved bill, and through
+  `GET /api/upiqr`.
+- **start / stop**: one-command dashboard launcher (pidfile-only lifecycle,
+  browser open, "already running" safe) — the recommended way to run shopkeep.
+- Dashboard language dropdown (English, हिन्दी, தமிழ், తెలుగు, বাংলা).
+- Self-tests grew from 28 to **41** (quickbill parity, import
+  all-or-nothing, report-vs-summary, scan degradation, UPI URI, start/stop
+  lifecycle, add-dup / edit / config / void / backup pairs, version
+  consistency).
+
+### Changed
+- README rewritten around the shop-owner workflow (start-first) with a full
+  button→endpoint→subcommand map and HTTP API reference.
+- `shellcheck` clean across the whole script (no new finding classes vs the
+  5A baseline); `--doctor` now reports scan/QR dependencies.
 
